Torchlight: what GLES2 shader compiles and links cost the calling thread, for
the game's log. With glthread (patches/mesa) the driver compiles on its worker,
and the game's thread waits for it at the status query that ends
GLSLESProgram::loadFromSource and each link; the wall time around them is what
a new shader costs the game. GLSLESShaderTimer adds it to
`ogre_gles2_shader_stats` (extern "C", read and reset by render/gl_thread.cpp
once a log window). The separable pipeline's compileAndLink is not timed itself:
it links through linkSeparable, which is. Not __SWITCH__-guarded: the GLES2
render system is built for the devices only, and both want the figure.


